Author: Moritz Thüning <moritz.thuening@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Aug 10 13:14:31 2026 +0000

    fix(protenix): free the h=1.5 normed pair tensor, closing the [385,506] crash band
    
    Every failure in the band throws at the same call, AttentionPairBias q@k^T
    (tenstorrent.py:2270 -> batched_matmul), seventeen lines below the
    _l1_layer_norm(z, 1.5) whose output is holding the banks. The Python frames were
    already in z-size-robustness' committed failure JSON; no instrument was needed.
    
    The normed pair tensor is dead at `z = zb`, but a rebind is not a free you can
    rely on: held L1 per bank at the throw tracks the norm's own padded footprint at
    385, 448, 480 and 506 to within the allocator's interleave rounding, and the bias
    permute is then placed underneath it, so the low-water mark stays low. Freeing it
    before the permute allocates lets the permute take the space instead.
    
    The circular-buffer side is now closed-form. _batched_matmul_search plans
    2*(p+Nt)*block_w*2048 + p*Nt*6144 plus 111104 B of fixed ttnn overhead, with
    p = per_core_M from the divisor structure of Nt and the 32-block saturation rule.
    That reproduces all four measured CB regions to the byte (1255936 at Nt=13,
    799232 at 14, 653824 at 15, 995840 at 16) and all four core ranges via
    cores = 16*Nt/p rounded down to whole grid columns. held + CB > 1461760 predicts
    all eleven measured verdicts, 352 through 512.
    
    Measured on qb1 card 0, --fast, production defaults, three sizes covering both
    edges: 385 ok 112.4 s, 448 ok 82.3 s, 506 ok 156.3 s, all previously crashes, and
    524 of 524 h=1.5 layer_norm calls still on the L1 branch at every size. 448 comes
    out plDDT 0.820076 / CIF sha256 0bd38dcabaeb91a1, byte-identical to the
    L1-flags-off control.
    
    Release-gated, not merged: tenstorrent.py is reached by opendde, four openfold3_*
    modules and esmfold2.

